  },
  "description": "The Tube Screamer's heart, both halves of its RC4558: a non-inverting stage with two diodes in its feedback (IC1B; Drive VR1, gain 1 + (51k + Drive) / 4k7) that clip softly, then the passive low-pass and active Tone control (IC1A, VR2). Values and refs from ElectroSmash's \"Tube Screamer Circuit Analysis\" (electrosmash.com/tube-screamer-analysis), as the TS808 starter; RC4558 and 1N4148 for the JRC4558 and MA150, which the page lists as alternatives. Biased from a reference voltage (vref port: wire it to a Vref divider); C7 blocks it at the output.",
  "tags": [
    "gain",
    "clipping",
    "tone",
    "opamp",
    "ts808"
  ],
